I've confirmed this is a consistent, hard block. Every attempt to load any page on ups.com (homepage, shipping tools, rate calculators, across multiple paths and multiple retries) results in Akamai's bot-detection system returning a fake empty "application/blank" response that Playwright treats as a file download, rather than serving the actual page content. This happens regardless of the specific URL path, indicating it's a site-wide block based on the automated browser's fingerprint (detected as HeadlessChrome), not a problem with any particular page or my navigation approach.

Since I cannot get the UPS website to render at all, I cannot proceed to use the shipping calculator, enter the package details, or obtain a quote. I will stop here as instructed, since continuing is not possible without working around the bot-detection block (which is not a legitimate workaround within the scope of this task).

ANSWER: {"answer": "Unable to complete the task. Every attempt to load www.ups.com (homepage, /us/en/Home.page, /ship/, rate calculator URLs, etc.) was blocked by UPS's Akamai bot-detection system, which returned an empty 'application/blank' response (triggering a fake file download in the browser) instead of the actual page content. This occurred consistently across multiple retries and different URL paths, indicating the automated browser is being fingerprinted and blocked site-wide (the browser's user agent reports as HeadlessChrome). Since the UPS site never rendered, I could not reach the shipping rate/quote tool, enter the package details (5 lbs, 4x4x4 in, New York NY 10001 to Truckee CA 96162), or retrieve any shipping quote. No quote could be obtained."}

